EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:

This annexation application was submitted for 2,364.25 acres of land located to the southeast of
the intersection of E. College Drive and Avenue C. This application was submitted along with a
preliminary plat application so that the property could begin the process of being subdivided.

Much of the land is zoned County PUD, with a small section to the north of this proposed
annexation being zoned County A-2 Agricultural. The applicants received conditional approval of
a City PUD preliminary plan from the Governing Body in 2016.

The applicants have proposed that this annexed land be a mix of residential, commercial, and
recreational uses. According to the impact assessment submitted with the preliminary plat
application, the project is expected to be built-out in five-year phases. By full build-out in the
year 2068, Sweetgrass is expected to have 5,000 dwelling units and 4,415,000 square feet of
non-residential floor area constructed. Based on the size and location of the project,
infrastructure and service impacts are expected. This annexation petition is a step in preparing
this land for that development.

PlanCheyenne supports this annexation application. The vast majority of the subject land is
located within the Urban Service Boundary and the subject land outside of the boundary is
proposed to be used as open space, trails, and passive recreational areas, which is consistent
with PlanChyenne. This application meets the requirements of Wyoming State Statute’s Title 15
and the associated petition was certified by the City Clerk as valid.

Due to meeting the review criteria found in Wyoming State 15-1-402, staff
recommends conditional approval of this annexation with five (5) recommended
conditions:

1. Correct or remove the “Note to Assessor” section per comments made by the County
Assessor and Planning and Development staff.
2. Correct the boundary measurements, per comments by the City Surveyor.
3. Correct the legal description to show a full metes and bounds description, per comments
by the City Surveyor.
4. Provide the boundary data for the W1/2 of Section 14 and the NE1/4NE1/4 of Section 15.
5. Add “a portion of Section 9” to the title block to match the entitlement of the associated
ordinance.
```

