PLANCHEYENNE - The application is in accordance with
the development policies and physical patterns identified
in the Comprehensive Plan.
This annexation is consistent with PlanCheyenne. The
vast majority of this land is within the Urban Service
Boundary (USB) and, per Policy 1.2.B, is encouraged to
develop with an urban character, however, some
portions of the annexation are outside of the current
USB. Policy 1.2.A explains that the USB is meant to
guide urban growth and distinguish between urban and
rural places.
Map #3, to the right, shows the current configuration of
the USB line in relation to the land that is the subject of
this annexation petition. The USB line is shown as a
green line and the area shaded in pink denotes the
subject land that is outside of the USB.
Based on the PUD preliminary plan and submitted
preliminary plat, the applicants intend those areas
outside the USB to be open space, trails, and portions of
a planned golf course, which is consistent with the intent
of the USB and Principle 1.2, which specifies that major
growth should take place within the USB to promote
efficient long-term use of land and urban services.
The subject land has several future land use
designations, shown in Table #1 below with the
percentage of the subject land designated with every
future land use category. Map #4 shows the location of
each of these designations with the subject land outlined
in red. The vast majority of the land is either designed
Urban Residential or Rural Residential. The submitted
preliminary plat shows a different configuration of land
uses than that of the current future land use map. It is
anticipated that the applicants may submit for a future
land use map amendment when their plans for the area
are finalized.
The applicants are seeking to zone this land to PUD
Planned Unit Development and have already received
conditional approval for the PUD preliminary plan from
the Governing Body. The applicants have not submitted
a PUD final plan to officially rezone the property to the
approved PUD.

